## Auth

`POST /auth/register` and `POST /auth/login` return `{ "token": "...", "user": { ... } }`.
The token is a compact `payload.signature` string signed with `APP_SECRET` (HMAC-SHA256) —
lightweight, self-contained, and **not** a full Symfony Security firewall. Send it back as
`Authorization: Bearer <token>` to reach `GET /auth/me`. Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes
via PHP's `password_hash()` and never returned.
